**Entra ID Objects and Role Based Access Control (RBAC)**

**Objective:**
Showcase the joiner part of identity lifecycle management and Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) using Microsoft Entra ID.

**This lab showcases:**
  -Manual user povisioning (joiner process)
  -Security group creation
  -Group-based access control
  -Role delegation using the principle of least privilege
---
**Scenario:**
There are three new users joining the organization (note these users are ficticious and not based on any singular person(s)):
  - Adam Grey: Controller
  - Denise Sutton: Talent Acquisition Specialist
  - Lily Polk: System Support Specialist
These three users will need corporate accounts along with being added to the correct security group.
---
**IAM Concept: Joiner**
A "Joiner" is the process taken to onboard a new employee and granting the necessary permissions to allow them to do their job while also exercising the principle of least privilege.

**Creating Users**
*Note, please see the Screenshots folder for pictures regarding this process

Standard Users:
  -agrey@tenant.onmicrosoft.com
  -dsutton@tenant.onmicrosoft.com
  -lpolk@tenant.onmicrosoft.com

IT Admin User:
  -polkl@tenant.onmicrosoft.com

**Configuration Steps**
Path: EntraID Admin Center -> Users -> New User

For each user: 
  -Identity type: Cloud-only
  -Assigned location
  -Temporary password generated
  -Require the password to be changed during the first login

**Security Considerations**
  -Unique credentials for each user
  -No accounts shared between users
  -The account with IT admin credentials was created as a separate account compared to the user's daily account. It is important have these accounts separate so the admin account is only used in situations where admin access is required.
